{"type":"text","timestamp":1794307017228,"sessionID":"ses_e3b02d0aaffe7caIqS0oXp2hoz","part":{"id":"prt_1c507faa3001UluwDqG74T37K8","sessionID":"ses_e3b02d0aaffe7caIqS0oXp2hoz","messageID":"msg_1c507e88c001wC0GV2MXUiz7pp","type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes made:\n\n1. **`todo/model.py`** — Added `priority: str = \"normal\"` field to the `Task` dataclass.\n\n2. **`todo/store.py`** — Updated `load()` to handle both the old format (bare JSON list, treating those tasks as `normal` priority) and the new `{\"version\": 2, \"tasks\": [...]}` format. Raises `ValueError` for any other version. `save()` always writes version 2 format.\n\n3. **`todo/cli.py`** — Added `--priority` option to the `add` subparser (choices: `low`, `normal`, `high`; default: `normal`; invalid values exit with status 2 via argparse). Added `--sort` option to the `list` subparser. List output now shows `(priority)` suffix for non-normal tasks and sorts by priority (high → normal → low, then by ascending id) when `--sort priority` is given.","time":{"start":1794306996899,"end":1794307017228}}}
